{0 ocsipersist-dbm}

DBM backend for Ocsipersist.
For the API documentation see OPAM package {{:../ocsipersist/Ocsipersist/index.html}ocsipersist}.
This page describes how to configure the DBM backend.
The DBM backend uses a server process [ocsidbm].

{1 Using as a library}

If you are not using Ocsigen Server's configuration file,
add library [ocsipersist-dbm.settings] in your Dune file, and
use module {!Ocsipersist_settings}
to configure the storage directory.
The directory is required: there is no default. Set it before
[Ocsipersist.init ()], otherwise it fails with an error asking for it.
By default, ocsidbm writes its errors to the standard error of the program;
{!Ocsipersist_settings.set_error_log_path} sends them to a file instead.

[Ocsipersist.init ()] connects to ocsidbm: the database can be accessed
only after it. Creating a persistent reference, a [Store_json] value or a
table does not access the database: it is accessed at the first [get],
[set], [find] or other use of the value. So these values can be created
before [Ocsipersist.init ()], for instance when a module is initialised.
[Store.make_persistent] accesses the database when called. An access made
before [Ocsipersist.init ()] fails, without breaking the value: the next
access tries again.

{[
let () =
  Ocsipersist_settings.set_store "data/store";
  Ocsipersist.init ()
]}

{1 Using with Ocsigen Server: ocsipersist-dbm-config}

If you want to configure Ocsipersist-dbm from Ocsigen Server's
configuration file, use package
{{:../ocsipersist-dbm-config/Ocsipersist_config/index.html}ocsipersist-dbm-config}.
